//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
// A compile reports what is wrong with the program it was asked to build, not with the library
// that program imports. `jobs_library_with_a_flaw` holds a function this file never calls whose
// body does not type check; the import is there for `library_good` alone.
//
// Both driver paths run the same checks here, so both RUN lines carry the same assertions: `-j`
// used to walk every module and report all of it, which refused this program while the default
// driver built it.
//
// RUN: vxc -j 4 --emit-mlir %s 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
// RUN: vxc --emit-mlir %s 2>&1 | FileCheck %s

import tests::modules::jobs_library_with_a_flaw;

fn main() -> i32 {
  return library_good(41);
}

// The library's flaw is not this compile's to report.
// CHECK-NOT: Undefined function
// The program still compiles, which is the half a silenced diagnostic could otherwise hide.
// CHECK: func.func @main
